{
  "base_commit": "cc18637d9fa01000867c0787aa01cc18348552cb",
  "scope": "Monte Carlo card-scene round states, timer/progress fields, rendering locals and corrected behavior comments.",
  "changes": [
    "Rename the three signed halfwords unk_60a8/60aa/60ae to mRoundState, mRoundTimer and mRoundProgress, preserving storage and offsets.",
    "Name round states1..8 from the existing play/exit switches; keep sequential state increments and the separate existing CardState enum.",
    "Clarify tile/palette, hidden-card traversal, visible-card count, reveal limit, selected-pair, credits, frame-index and flip-slot locals.",
    "Correct comments for the exit timer return, absolute vertical movement step, bit3 blink mask and new-touch-edge requirement.",
    "Format implementations consistently without changing order, scopes, null guards, cached pointers or lifecycle construction."
  ],
  "evidence": {
    "progress": "mRoundProgress receives dealer signals through Dealer_StartDeal/Dealer_StartReveal. Initial deal multiplies it by5 and waits for4; play uses it for the reveal limit. Exit clears it and uses it as the count of cards already hidden while walking backward from the tail. The shared name reflects these separate uses.",
    "states": "Round values1..3 implement prompt setup, initial deal and play;4..8 free graphics, wait for the dealer, hide cards, flip cards and run the exit delay. The scene state remains s16; no state0 meaning is invented.",
    "comments": "ApproachLinear2(short&,short,short) in src/ApproachAngle.cpp returns1 on reaching the target. Exit state8 returns1 when its timer reaches0; state7 separately returns1 while active credits are nonzero. Rendering tests absolute mYStep>0, not upward direction. Card blinking tests mask8, which is bit3. HitTest requires both gTouchHeld and gTouchEdge.",
    "ownership": "Queue30 state5803e2a26b3c986b2de0039a344eda7c16202bca has no active scene/card/shared-state class, source/header or complete-range conflicts. Production ov006 ranges:text0x020f7634..0x020f8ef4,init0x021318a0..0x0213195c,ctor0x021335b8..0x021335bc,bss0x0214250c..0x02142558. Header has one consumer.",
    "runtime_validation": "No new emulator claim: the field names and comment corrections follow explicit accesses, helper return semantics and arithmetic. Global resource identities and visual animation names remain unchanged.",
    "retained_constraints": [
      "Keep manual factory, shared partial-state wrapper, inline scene destructor/key-function ownership, reverse ROM source order and generated metadata.",
      "Keep delta[3] for the two-dimensional subtraction, the saved list head captured before unlinking, separate null guards and rereads, and mArray[76].mTargetY address formation for the unused reset argument.",
      "Keep existing helper/global names, scalar ABI declarations, list operations, card-state constants, raw resource IDs and shared dealer fields. The MCarlo2 sibling and common dealer headers are untouched."
    ]
  },
